$ A cantilevered flat plate: 6061-like aluminium (E 70 GPa, nu 0.33,
$ rho 2700 kg/m^3), chord 0.2 m along x, span 0.5 m along y, 2 mm thick,
$ clamped along its root at y = 0, in the x-y plane. 4 x 8 CQUAD4 (45
$ grids) and one CAERO1 panel of the same 4 x 8 boxes on a surface spline,
$ the wall at the root a reflection plane (symmetric about x-z), so the
$ aerodynamics see a wing of aspect ratio 5. SI units, sea level air
$ (1.225 kg/m^3).
$
$ The three decks flat_plate_sol144.dat, flat_plate_sol145.dat and
$ flat_plate_sol146.dat share the model, the flight point (40 m/s, q = 980
$ Pa, Mach 0.1) and these numbers, so each checks the others:
$   * SOL 144 trims the plate at an angle of attack of 1/40 rad, which is
$     what a 1 m/s vertical gust does at 40 m/s and zero frequency; its tip
$     deflection is the limit of SOL 146's gust response as f -> 0.
$   * SOL 144's DIVERG gives the divergence dynamic pressure; SOL 145's PK
$     sweep finds the same divergence as a root going to zero frequency.
$ The fork's standalone/test/run_decks.py runs the three and checks both.
$
$ SOL 146: the plate's response to a vertical gust at 40 m/s, Mach 0.1:
$ the harmonic response to a 1 m/s gust from 0.5 to 80 Hz (WG = 1/40,
$ the frequency dependence a TABLED1 of 1.0), and through RANDOM a von
$ Karman gust of 1 m/s rms and 2.5 m scale length, its PSD and rms at
$ the tip. 2% structural damping.
SOL 146
CEND
TITLE = flat plate, SOL 146 gust response
ECHO = SORT
SPC = 1
METHOD = 1
SDAMPING = 40
FREQ = 41
DLOAD = 42
GUST = 42
RANDOM = 45
$ the tip, at the leading edge, mid-chord and trailing edge
SET 101 = 41,43,45
DISP = 101
SUBCASE 1
  SUBTITLE = 1 m/s vertical gust, 40 m/s, Mach 0.1
OUTPUT(XYPLOT)
XYPRINT DISP PSDF / 41(T3), 43(T3), 45(T3)
BEGIN BULK
PARAM,LMODES,6
PARAM,Q,980.0
PARAM,MACH,0.1
$ the gust aerodynamics computed (MSC's spelling; the front end flips the sign)
PARAM,GUSTAERO,-1
$ the plate: x chordwise (the flow), y spanwise, z up; grid 1 + i + 5 j
$ (i = 0..4 along the chord, j = 0..8 along the span), quad 1 + i + 4 j
$ in-plane freedoms and the drilling rotation out (GRID PS 126)
GRID,1,,0.0,0.0,0.0,,126
GRID,2,,0.05,0.0,0.0,,126
GRID,3,,0.1,0.0,0.0,,126
GRID,4,,0.15,0.0,0.0,,126
GRID,5,,0.2,0.0,0.0,,126
GRID,6,,0.0,0.0625,0.0,,126
